    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch03-02: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.73";
    dc:description "Spread data are extensive, but paired fertility and mortality data are available only for selected invasions. Thus exponential spread is testable broadly while the asserted exclusive demographic explanation is only partially resolvable.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: For dated introductions, fit spread and abundance trajectories using intrinsic growth, fertility in native versus introduced ranges, and stage-specific mortality. Rapid spread explained by reduced mortality without increased fertility supports the claim.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "A specific dataset URL may not encode abundance or demography.", "Enemy release, adaptation and propagule pressure are confounded.", "Introduction dates and early absences are uncertain.";
